# Auto-upload to GitHub

After you finish a set of file changes the user asked for, commit and push to `origin` on `main`. Do not wait for them to say "push". This is an explicit project preference.

- One commit per finished request, not per keystroke or half-written file
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, passwords, API keys)
- If `git` is missing from PATH, use `C:\Program Files\Git\cmd\git.exe`
- Remote: `https://github.com/theharislt-netizen/garage-gains.git`

Pushing to GitHub **is** editing the files in the repo. Do not tell the user to re-download `garage-gains.html` after an update. A new download is a new blank local profile. Workout points, items, and the Harris/Haris save live in the phone browser, not in GitHub. Opening the repo in the GitHub app is enough to view the updated code.

The app title is **RIGCORE**. The file name is `garage-gains.html`. All progress is localStorage key `garageGains_v1` as one JSON object. Never rename that key, never break the original save shape, and keep Settings Export/Import Backup working. Browser storage is scoped to the file path, not the app version.
